Well I finally tracked down the major problem in compiling nethack
with the new 2.3.1 compiler from SCO, apparently the new compiler
handles the const type differently than the old one. so the
declarations of such things such as the array vowels does not 
get passed to all the modules even though there is an extern statment
the only way I have found around this so far is to do a   
#define const
and compile with out the arrays being a const.


